// WGMMA reads its B operand as core matrices of 8 rows x 16 B, and the 16 B
// always span the contraction axis.  K contracts over the feature dim, V over
// the key index, so V is staged transposed:
//
//   K (k = dim):  il (key,dim) = (key>>3)*1024 + (dim>>3)*64 + (key&7)*8 + (dim&7)
//   V (k = key):  ilt(key,dim) = (key>>3)*1024 + (dim>>3)*64 + (dim&7)*8 + (key&7)
//
// Both use LBO = 2048 B (key-block stride) and SBO = 128 B (dim-block stride).
// A 64-key stage advances the K base by 128 halves and the V base by 2048 halves.
